  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nI have a homarr group called \"admins\" with admin privileges.\n\nIn Keycloak, in Client scopes -> roles -> mappers -> roles, the \"client roles\" mapper has a Token Claim Name of `resource_access.${client_id}.roles`.\n\nIf I create a client called \"homarr\" and add a role called \"admins\" to it, the `/userinfo` endpoint returns this\n```\n\"resource_access\":{\"homarr\":{\"roles\":[\"admins\"]}\n```\n\nI set the environment variable `AUTH_OIDC_GROUPS_ATTRIBUTE` to be `resource_access.homarr.roles`, but this does not assign the user to the \"admins\" group.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nElaborated in the description.\n\n### Impact\n\nThis prevents the use of client roles in Keycloak.\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version\n\n1.11.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
  "closed_by": null,
